{"causes": ["The fragmentation of the Piast dynasty into numerous Silesian duchies created a complex web of independent and semi-independent rulers.", "The inheritance customs of the Piast family, which often led to the division of territories among male heirs, defined the scope of Konrad V's initial rule.", "The escalating religious and political tensions leading to the Hussite Wars profoundly destabilized Central Europe and directly impacted Silesian ducal policies."], "effects": ["Konrad V Kantner's rule ensured the continuity of the Oleśnica branch of the Silesian Piasts through a turbulent period.", "His involvement, directly or indirectly, in the Hussite Wars contributed to the regional dynamics and defensive strategies of Silesian duchies.", "His death led to the further division of the Duchy of Oleśnica between his sons, Konrad IX the Black and Konrad X the White."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "konrad-v-kantner", "sourceName": "Konrad V Kantner", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "hussite-wars", "targetName": "Hussite Wars", "context": "Konrad V Kantner, like other Silesian dukes, was compelled to engage with or defend against the Hussite forces during his reign (1412–1439)."}, {"sourceSlug": "konrad-v-kantner", "sourceName": "Konrad V Kantner", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "duchy-of-olesnica", "targetName": "Duchy of Oleśnica", "context": "Konrad V Kantner ruled as Duke of Oleśnica, making it the primary seat of his power during his lifetime."}, {"sourceSlug": "konrad-iii-the-old", "sourceName": "Konrad III the Old", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "konrad-v-kantner", "targetName": "Konrad V Kantner", "context": "As Konrad V Kantner's father, Konrad III the Old established the lineage and territorial claims that his son would inherit in 1412."}, {"sourceSlug": "wladyslaw-ii-jagiello", "sourceName": "Władysław II Jagiełło", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "konrad-v-kantner", "targetName": "Konrad V Kantner", "context": "As the powerful King of Poland, Władysław II Jagiełło exerted significant regional influence over Silesian dukes like Konrad V Kantner, particularly in the context of Hussite threats."}, {"sourceSlug": "konrad-ix-the-black", "sourceName": "Konrad IX the Black", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "konrad-v-kantner", "targetName": "Konrad V Kantner", "context": "Konrad IX the Black, along with his brother Konrad X the White, inherited and divided the Duchy of Oleśnica upon the death of their father, Konrad V Kantner, in 1439."}], "places": [{"name": "Oleśnica, Poland", "role": "Seat of Power"}, {"name": "Wrocław, Poland", "role": "Regional Capital"}, {"name": "Prague, Czech Republic", "role": "Hussite Center"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Konrad V Kantner", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "konrad-v-kantner"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q557484", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Konrad_V_Kantner"], "tags": ["Germany", "Monarchs & Rulers", "Europe", "political-systems", "empire-and-colonialism", "geopolitical-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 5, "significanceNarrative": "Konrad V Kantner's rule as Duke of Oleśnica maintained a regional Piast lineage through the tumultuous Hussite Wars, contributing to the complex political landscape of late medieval Silesia and ensuring dynastic continuity for his sons.", "significanceCategory": "local"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-09-26T07:19:33Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#36226198124", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Konrad V Kantner was a duke of Oleśnica, Koźle, half of Bytom and half of Ścinawa during 1412–1427, since 1427 sole ruler over Oleśnica.", "newValue": "Konrad V Kantner, a member of the Silesian Piast dynasty, reigned as Duke of Oleśnica, Koźle, half of Bytom, and half of Ścinawa from 1412 until his death in 1439. Initially sharing power with his brothers, he emerged as the sole ruler of the Duchy of Oleśnica after 1427, a period marked by significant political fragmentation and the turbulent Hussite Wars in Central Europe. His rule represented a continuation of the Piast legacy in a highly contested region, navigating the complex allegiances and shifting power dynamics between the Bohemian Crown, the Polish Kingdom, and various Silesian duchies.

During his co-regency with brothers Konrad IV the Elder, Konrad VI the Dean, Konrad VII the Old White, and Konrad VIII the Younger, Konrad V participated in the intricate feudal politics of Silesia. Following the death of his elder brothers and the division of territories, he consolidated his control over Oleśnica, an important strategic and economic center. His reign coincided with the Hussite Wars (1419–1434), which profoundly impacted Silesia; Konrad V, like many Silesian dukes, was compelled to contend with Hussite incursions and occasionally formed alliances, often defensive, against the radical Bohemian reformers, while maintaining a delicate balance between Catholic loyalty and pragmatic regional survival.

Konrad V's legacy is primarily one of dynastic continuity and regional stability amidst widespread upheaval. His ability to retain control over Oleśnica and pass it to his sons, Konrad IX the Black and Konrad X the White, ensured the persistence of this branch of the Piast dynasty for another generation. His rule, though not marked by grand conquests or sweeping reforms, exemplified the challenges faced by minor nobility in maintaining their sovereignty and patrimony during a period of intense religious and political strife, contributing to the complex tapestry of late medieval Silesian history."}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-26T07:19:33Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#36226198124", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1380"}, {"title": "Dynastic succession and sovereign authority traditions", "type": "Idea", "year": "1380"}], "newValue": ["The fragmentation of the Piast dynasty into numerous Silesian duchies created a complex web of independent and semi-independent rulers.", "The inheritance customs of the Piast family, which often led to the division of territories among male heirs, defined the scope of Konrad V's initial rule.", "The escalating religious and political tensions leading to the Hussite Wars profoundly destabilized Central Europe and directly impacted Silesian ducal policies."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-26T07:19:33Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#36226198124", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Established dynastic legacies and territorial boundaries", "type": "Idea", "year": "1439-09-10"}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "year": "1439-09-10"}], "newValue": ["Konrad V Kantner's rule ensured the continuity of the Oleśnica branch of the Silesian Piasts through a turbulent period